A||||3||Hippocrat||All fieros have the same dimensions?||||5||
Z||000000||Hippocrat||09-21-2001||02:08 AM||||Looks to me like the answer should be yes but I have to ask.<P>Are all fieros built on the same space frames<BR>For example .. can I bolt a gt nose clip on an SE .. <P>In general I guess the question is are all body panels interchangeable? <BR>Even if its with in styles e.g. all notch backs and all fast backs.<P>Sorry if it seems obvious but hey.. I gotta Know for sure<P>Thanx.<P>A search of the archives turned up some info saying that all the side panels (fenders doors and even hoods) are pretty much the same. <BR>Only the Front and rear fascias are tricky.<BR>everyone agree? or disagree?<p>[This message has been edited by Hippocrat (edited 09-21-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-21-2001||04:36 AM||||Yes and no.  Yes, everything will bolt up to the same spaceframe.  All of the spaceframes were identical.  However, you will have to change a few minor parts if your adding or subtracting certain parts.  For example, if you're adding the aero front fascia to an originally non aero car, you'll need to swap out the wheel wells and (I think) the front fenders (could be wrong about this).  You also have to switch the side molding if you go with later style GT type fascias if you want everything to match.  The door skins, fenders and 1/4 panels are slightly different on some of the models as they have provisions for the ground fx, but you can always drill your own mounting holes or go without ground fx.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hippocrat||09-21-2001||04:41 AM||||Thanx for the input .. pretty much what I'm seeing in the archive. Basically theres not to much that cant be manipulated then? (drilling holes is the fun part)<BR>moldings seem to be the only real factor. ||||reg||7
Z||000003||mbramble||09-21-2001||07:00 AM||||All fenders are the same except for the holes in those that have ground f/x.  As MM said, you can drill them yourself if you want to put ground f/x on a fender, doorskin, or rear quarter panel that didn't have them originally.  If you are swapping to a different style of fascia, you need to also get the impact absorber from the donor and get every piece that attaches the fascia to the frame of the donor car.  The different styles have different mounting pieces and to do the job right you need all the stuff from the donor.||||reg||1
